us 32:9 (God's word), 33:3, 33:5 (the ornaments), 34:9 (Moses' plea); 9:6 and 9:13 here (Moses' word and God's quoted)", 'the_nape': 11, 'the_state': 'no write, no entry — the one database scanned on israel_people: []', 'the_shelf': 'Beitzah 25b:7-8 — the stiff neck the REASON the Torah was given (impudence); the three impudent ones', 'onkelos': "'קשי קדל' (hard of neck) at 9:6 and 9:13"}; the_three_voices_on_one_pronoun = {'the_finding': "the second person SINGULAR in twelve verses — 1-6 ISRAEL (Moses to the people), 12 and 14 GOD'S 'you' to Moses (the divine frames), 26-29 MOSES' 'You' to God (the prayer); PLURAL in twelve (8-10, 16-19, 21-25); BOTH at 9:7 alone (the switch inside the verse); NEITHER at 11, 13, 15, 20", 'the_register': ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 12, 14, 26, 27, 28, 29], [8, 9, 10, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25], [7], [11, 13, 15, 20])}; taberah_outside_the_ten = {'the_list': ('two_at_the_sea', 'two_at_the_water', 'two_at_the_manna', 'two_at_the_quail', 'one_at_the_calf', 'one_at_paran'), 'the_chapters_four': "Massah = the second water (Rephidim, Arakhin 15a:20), Kibroth-hattaavah = the second quail (15a:14), Horeb's calf (9:8) = the calf, Kadesh-barnea (9:23) = Paran — the tenth that sealed the sentence (15a:10)", 'taberah': "9:22's first name — NOT among the ten (Arakhin 15a:14); Berakhot 32a:5's impertinence its row (the al-tikrei ('do not read') el/al)", 'the_finding': "the retelling names a provocation the answer sheet's list does not — the design did not predict it (the docket's find)"}; the_merit_of_the_fathers = {'the_plea': "9:27 'remember Your servants, Abraham, Isaac and Jacob' — Exodus 32:13's; Berakhot 32a:17 the three-legged chair (the fathers' merit); 32a:24 the oath by the Name endures", 'the_two_arms': 'Shabbat 55a:11 — the letter tav: SHMUEL — tama, the merit of the Patriarchs has CEASED; R. YOCHANAN — tachon, He will have mercy by it on the righteous', 'the_four_dates': "55a:13-16 — from when did it cease? Rav: Hosea's days (Hosea 2:12); Shmuel: Hazael's (2 Kings 13:23 — 'His covenant with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob, and would not destroy them': THE LAST TIME); R. Yehoshua ben Levi: Elijah's (1 Kings 18:36); R. Yochanan: Hezekiah's (Isaiah 9:6)", 'the_kin': "2 Kings 13:23's 'would not destroy them … His covenant with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob' the run's kin of 9:26-27"}; the_crowns_of_horeb = {'the_row': "Shabbat 88a:7 — R. Simai: at 'we will do' before 'we will hear' 600,000 angels tied two crowns to each Israelite; AT THE CALF 1,200,000 angels of destruction REMOVED them — 'the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments from Mount Horeb' (Exodus 33:6); R. Chama: at Horeb put on, at Horeb removed", 'the_tape': 'Exodus 33:1-6 has NO LINE (the tent pitched outside, 33:7-11, the only Exodus 33 line): the crowns a status the calf removed, never written', 'the_chapter': "9:8 'at Horeb you provoked' — the two Horebs of this row"}; the_asymmetry_megillah_4_10 = {'the_rule': "Mishnah Megillah 4:10 — the first calf account (Exodus 32:1-20) read and translated; the SECOND — Aaron's report (32:21-24) — read and NOT translated (Megillah 25b:11 the boundary; 25b:12 'this calf came out' the heretics' opening)", 'the_asymmetry': "Deuteronomy's own telling of Aaron's peril (9:20) IS translated — Onkelos 9:20 read whole at sitting 7: the retelling escapes the rule that guards Aaron's report", 'the_cell': 'second_read_not_translated'}; the_three_requests = {'the_rows': "Berakhot 7a:23-25 — Moses requested three things after the calf and all were granted (R. Yochanan in R. Yosei's name): the Presence to rest on Israel, not on the nations (33:16), the ways of God revealed (33:13); 7a:29 — R. Meir: two granted, the ways not (33:19)", 'the_tape': "Exodus 33:12-23 has NO LINE (the tent pitched outside the only Exodus 33 line): the three requests inside the second forty's stretch, unwritten", 'the_timing': "Berakhot 7a:5 — do not placate a person in his anger: 'My face will go' (33:14) — the second forty waited out"}; the_tablets_size = {'the_parameter': (6, 6, 3), 'the_row': "Nedarim 38a:8 — the tablets six handbreadths long, six wide, three thick: Moses' might read from 9:17's own verbs ('I took hold … and threw them from my two hands'); Pesachim 87b:22 the letters flew back", 'the_ark': "the fragments in the ark — Menachot 99a:12; Bava Batra 14b:4-7; erection.tablets('fragments_by_call') = both_in_the_ark; the entry OWED to chapter 10"}; the_calfs_debt = {'the_surcharge': "Sanhedrin 102a:15 — one twenty-fourth of the surplus of a litra of the first calf in every punishment (Exodus 32:34 'on the day when I punish'); 102a:16 — collected after twenty-four generations (Ezekiel 9:1); erection.calf('surcharge') = one_twenty_fourth", 'the_forgetting': "Berakhot 32b:15-19 — 'THESE too shall be forgotten' (Isaiah 49:15): the sin of the calf; 'I will not forget you' — Sinai", 'the_registers': 'two registers on the shelf — the debt OPEN against the sin FORGOTTEN — neither on the tape; the tension recorded, not resolved', 'di_zahav': 'Berakhot 32a:8, 32a:13 — the wealth caused it, and God conceded it (Hosea 2:10)'}; the_provocations_order = {'the_retelling': 'Taberah, Massah, Kibroth-hattaavah (9:22 — one verse, three names), Kadesh-barnea (9:23)', 'the_tape': "named 'Massah and Meribah' (Exod 17:7), fire_of_the_lord_burned (Num 11:1 — Taberah), quail_and_plague (11:31 — Kibroth), congregation_wept (14:1 — Kadesh)", 'the_days': "the tape's lines carry their own days — M['taberah'] the march + 3 (Ta'anit 29a:3), M['hazeroth'] (29a:4), M['spies_return'] (2, 5, 9) (29a:5-7): Mishnah Ta'anit 4:6's second list proved as 28b:8-10 proved the first"}; the_uncited_verses = [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 13, 15, 16, 18, 20, 22, 23, 24, 28, 29]; the_credits = {'the_erection': "the calf's rows credited from the erection's docket (Berakhot 32a:14-24, 7a:5, 7a:23-25; Shabbat 87a:5, 88a:7, 89a:6; Avodah Zarah 44a:2; Sanhedrin 102a:5, 102a:15; Yoma 86b:14; Menachot 99b:1; Ta'anit 28b:9-10,